<title>The Source Book — Ophan Tutor, Book I</title>
<style>
  :root { --bg:#050914; --card:#0a1428; --text:#e8f4f8; --gold:#d4af37; --cyan:#7fdbff; --border:#1a3350; }
  body { font-family: Georgia, serif; background: var(--bg); color: var(--text); margin:0; padding:20px; line-height:1.65; }
  .container { max-width: 720px; margin:auto; }
  h1 { color: var(--gold); text-align:center; font-size:1.7em; letter-spacing:1px; border-bottom:2px solid var(--gold); padding-bottom:12px; margin-bottom:4px; }
  .subtitle { text-align:center; color:var(--cyan); font-style:italic; font-size:0.9em; margin-bottom:6px; }
  .stamp { text-align:center; color:#557; font-size:0.7em; font-family:monospace; letter-spacing:1px; margin-bottom:30px; }
  h2 { color: var(--gold); font-size:1.15em; text-transform:uppercase; letter-spacing:1px; border-bottom:1px solid var(--border); padding-bottom:6px; margin-top:40px; }
  h3 { color: var(--cyan); font-size:1em; margin-bottom:4px; }
  .part { text-align:center; color:var(--gold); font-size:0.8em; letter-spacing:3px; text-transform:uppercase; margin:34px 0 10px; }
  .lib-item { background: var(--card); border:1px solid var(--border); border-left:3px solid var(--gold); border-radius:6px; padding:16px; margin-bottom:14px; }
  .lib-title { color: var(--gold); font-weight:bold; font-size:1.05em; margin-bottom:4px; }
  .lib-type { font-size:0.7em; color:var(--cyan); text-transform:uppercase; letter-spacing:1.5px; display:block; margin-bottom:8px; }
  .lib-desc { font-size:0.9em; color:#ccc; }
  .app { background: var(--card); border:1px solid var(--border); border-left:3px solid var(--cyan); border-radius:6px; padding:16px; margin-bottom:18px; }
  .app-tag { font-family:monospace; font-size:0.68em; color:var(--gold); background:#1a3350; padding:2px 7px; border-radius:4px; letter-spacing:1px; }
  table { width:100%; border-collapse:collapse; margin-top:10px; font-size:0.78em; }
  th, td { border:1px solid var(--border); padding:6px; text-align:left; vertical-align:top; }
  th { background:#0d1e38; color:var(--cyan); font-size:0.95em; }
  ul { padding-left:20px; } li { margin-bottom:7px; font-size:0.92em; }
  .commission { border:1px solid var(--cyan); background:#000; border-radius:6px; padding:16px; margin-top:40px; text-align:center; font-size:0.9em; }
  .resolved { font-size:0.84em; color:var(--cyan); margin-bottom:0; }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<div class="container">

  <h1>The Source Book</h1>
  <div class="subtitle">Ophan Tutor — Book I, Single Volume with Appendix</div>
  <div class="stamp">BUILD SB-1.1 · PART I UNALTERED · APPENDIX APPENDED · JUBILEE RESOLVED</div>

  <div class="part">Part I — The Seven Sources</div>
  <p style="font-size:0.85em; color:#888; font-style:italic;">Reproduced without alteration from the Source Library register. No entry has been edited, merged, reordered, or abridged.</p>

  <div class="lib-item">
    <div class="lib-title">New World Translation of the Holy Scriptures (1983)</div>
    <span class="lib-type">Primary Text</span>
    <div class="lib-desc">The default translation for all scriptural citations and the foundational authority for the Ophan Tutor.</div>
  </div>

  <div class="lib-item">
    <div class="lib-title">Insight on the Scriptures (Volumes 1 &amp; 2)</div>
    <span class="lib-type">Watchtower Publication</span>
    <div class="lib-desc">Used for deep lexical, historical, and theological verification. The source for the Hebrew Lexicon entries and the 24 elders / 144,000 administrative structure.</div>
  </div>

  <div class="lib-item">
    <div class="lib-title">Theocratic Ministry School Guidebook</div>
    <span class="lib-type">Watchtower Publication</span>
    <div class="lib-desc">The source for the teaching methodology. Instructs the speaker to use plain language, avoid haughtiness, and adapt to the audience.</div>
  </div>

  <div class="lib-item">
    <div class="lib-title">Learn From the Great Teacher</div>
    <span class="lib-type">Watchtower Publication</span>
    <div class="lib-desc">The source for the conversational entry protocol. Demonstrates how Jesus used simple illustrations and parables to explain deep truths.</div>
  </div>

  <div class="lib-item">
    <div class="lib-title">Life—How Did It Get Here? By Evolution or by Creation?</div>
    <span class="lib-type">Watchtower Publication</span>
    <div class="lib-desc">The source for the scientific and design arguments. Used when building the Physical Constants Engine (the 864/432 relationship).</div>
  </div>

  <div class="lib-item">
    <div class="lib-title">Revelation—Its Grand Climax At Hand!</div>
    <span class="lib-type">Watchtower Publication</span>
    <div class="lib-desc">The source for the 24 elders = 144,000 identification, the 24 divisions of 6,000, and the interpretation of the heavenly throne room.</div>
  </div>

  <div class="lib-item">
    <div class="lib-title">Strong's Exhaustive Concordance</div>
    <span class="lib-type">Reference Tool</span>
    <div class="lib-desc">Used for the Hebrew/Greek word numbers (H4060, H4150, H520, etc.) and the foundational lexical definitions in the Lexicon tab.</div>
  </div>

  <div class="part">Part II — The Appendage</div>
